    <h2>6. Gate-Depth Latency Comparison Chart</h2>
    <p>Combinational propagation delay scales with the critical-path depth of 2-input <code>Nand</code> stages from primary inputs to outputs. While basic gates resolve in 1–3 stages, the 16-bit ripple-carry <code>Add16</code> inside the Hack <code>ALU</code> dominates critical-path latency (32 NAND stages for carry propagation across 16 full adders), whereas <code>RAM64</code> read latency adds two levels of 8-way address decoding (<code>Mux8Way16</code>) atop the register output.</p>

